# Direct runtime dependencies of reranker-service (see pyproject.toml).
# torch is deliberately NOT listed here: the Dockerfile installs it
# separately from a configurable index (TORCH_INDEX_URL, CPU vs CUDA
# wheel) so the same lockfile serves both build variants; hash-pinning it
# here would fix it to one index/variant, defeating that toggle. This is a
# known, documented exception to issue #230's hash-pinning -- torch's own
# supply-chain risk is separately mitigated by pinning TORCH_INDEX_URL to a
# specific, air-gap-mirrorable index rather than a hash list.
# Compiled to requirements.txt with `pip-compile --generate-hashes`.
